# Cross-Project Product Boundary (Looma <-> Knit)

Looma is the official UI library of Knit, and also a general-purpose library for non-Knit apps.

Sibling app repository: `../knit`

## API Scope Rules

- Build reusable primitives and options first.
- Avoid domain-specific naming tied to Knit entities or routes.
- Support Knit through theming, composition, and examples, not domain-coupled APIs.

## Promotion Rules

- Promote generic components/options discovered in Knit usage.
- Keep Knit business logic and domain orchestration in `../knit`.
- Prefer additive APIs (slots/props/events) over app-specific branching.

## Docs Guidance

- Examples can subtly reflect Knit visual style and icon usage.
- Keep wording and API contracts framework- and app-agnostic.
